# Every tracked file is LF in the working copy as well as in the index, whatever
# core.autocrlf is set to. With core.autocrlf=true and no setting here, a Windows
# checkout is CRLF, and a `\r` at the end of each line reaches a shell hook as
# data: a line read with `while IFS= read -r` then differs from a `\r`-free
# expectation that prints the same.
* text=auto eol=lf
